 "notes": [
  "topology: source -> pool -> one sweep declaring a 120-frame window attention-first from its midpoint. Three landings per shape; the third is the metric. Ceiling 1.5 windows = 2.66 GB at 15.1 MB a frame, so half a window of victims is the most any policy can keep.",
  "core shape: 1 fetch thread, 1 reader, 2 recorders, no step and no interactive consumer \u2014 this measures retention, and a second consumer would make the decode counts a statement about scheduling as well.",
  "`drop-all` calls drop_unreferenced at each landing, which is V1's explorer. Every other arm lets the byte ceiling decide, which is what makes it a victim cache; the ceiling never fired in any V1 run, per the derived-eviction finding.",
  "seeks are reported beside decodes because a scattered remnant must be seeked through: fewer decodes at more seeks is the pre-registered way a per-item ranking fails here, since GreedyDual-Size treats items as independent and a frame's cost depends on whether its neighbour is resident.",
  "exact-return / drop-all: return leg decoded 120 of 120 rows in 1.544 s with 2 seeks; 0 rows were already resident on arrival, in 0 contiguous run(s), and 0 serves came from unpinned keys.",
